{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/planning/chunks/C{27,28,29,30,31,32,33}.md docs/planning/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md'","aggregated_output":"# C27 — UI v2 design specification and P09 registration\n\nPhase: P09. Status: planned. Required predecessor: C26 is not required; C27 is docs and controller registration only and may proceed in parallel with C26 (D058).\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe reviewed \"Refined Native\" prototype (canvas version 134) is extracted into a specification the remaining P09 chunks are judged against, and the review controller recognises P09.\n\n## Inputs and dependency gates\n\nD058; the six frozen R2 files and their SHA-256 manifest; the 16 Codex prototype review rounds (summarised in DESIGN-V2 §9).\n\nRead the [common execution contract](../IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md),\n[review protocol](../review-protocol.md), and [test catalogue](../test-catalogue.md).\nRead the [UI v2 specification](../../architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md) and its\ncompanions; the frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is\nan immutable input. Freeze all source/shared dependency inputs.\n\n## Milestones\n\n1. Write `docs/architecture/ui-v2/`: DESIGN-V2, tokens, state ownership, invariants with test ids, screen contracts, provenance, frozen prototype with manifest.\n2. Write chunk instructions C28–C34, the P09 row in the implementation plan, the chunk index, the status row and D058.\n3. Register P09 in the controller: `Subject` accepts C27–C34 and P09; `checks.json` gains C27–C34 entries and P09; C27 is marked `docs_only`, which the controller enforces as: no native-prepare run, no native inventory or acceptance (also excluded from P09's integrated native members), and owner acceptance below 9/10 refused at completion and at completion recognition. Application chunks keep every gate: a missing or empty native inventory still fails, and marking an application chunk `docs_only` is rejected by manifest validation. Production controller paths and these refusals are tested.\n4. Request independent Codex review of the specification at the 9/10 bar.\n\n## Required acceptance\n\n- The specification assigns every prototype state field (state-ownership.md), names twelve invariants each with at least one test id, and lists every deviation from the prototype in provenance.md.\n- `cargo test -p xtask --lib` and the `shell_controller` suite pass with the controller changes; `Subject::parse(\"C34\")` and `\"P09\"` succeed; `\"C35\"` and `\"P10\"` are refused; `required_runs(C27)` has no native-prepare; `owner_acceptance_allowed(C27)` and `(P09)` refuse; `native_members(P09)` excludes C27; mutation \"application chunk marked docs_only\" is rejected.\n- The specification maps every product, tab and action to an admitted service or marks it unavailable (DESIGN-V2 §6); the state inventory lists every `s.*`, `ts.*` and `f.*` key of the frozen prototype; every behavioural deviation is in provenance.md with its owning chunk.\n- No application source outside `crates/xtask` and the checks/native-checks manifests changes in this chunk.\n\n## Evidence and completion\n\nReview packet for C27 under `reviews/C27/`. Require ≥9/10 overall and in every dimension (this chunk is excluded from the D034 8/10 allowance because every later chunk depends on it). Preserve attempts, raw verdicts, hashes and remediation. Commit only the reviewed tree.\n\n## Safety and recovery\n\nDocs and controller only. While C26 is incomplete the controller refuses to review C27 (predecessor gate), so C27 is reviewed through the fresh-exec fallback by hand with the same prompt and verdict schema, with a source-bound run record under `evidence/C27/runs/`; the receipt is regenerated through the controller once C26 completes, before C28 starts.\n# C28 — Tokens, v2 shell behind the flag, Home skeleton\n\nPhase: P09. Status: planned. Required predecessor: C27 and C26.\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe new shell (sidebar with tenant switcher, navigation inventory, native shortcuts, palette, toasts, modal stack, theme) renders behind a Rust-owned `ui_variant` flag with a Home skeleton, and the legacy shell is untouched.\n\n## Inputs and dependency gates\n\nC27 specification. Read the [common execution contract](../IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md),\n[review protocol](../review-protocol.md), and [test catalogue](../test-catalogue.md).\nRead the [UI v2 specification](../../architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md) and its\ncompanions; the frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is\nan immutable input. Freeze all source/shared dependency inputs.\n\n## Milestones\n\n1. `ShellSnapshot.ui_variant` and `onboarding` fields; `FeatureId::{Home, Inbox}`; one navigation inventory (label, shortcut index, sidebar membership, availability) consumed by the native menu, sidebar and palette; `navigate` intent; ts-rs regeneration.\n2. `apps/desktop/src/styles/tokens.css` per tokens.md; `data-theme` from the observed appearance; no inline colours.\n3. Shell components: sidebar (collapsing below 1280px), tenant switcher (switch intent only; guard dialog deferred to C30 but the refusal type is defined), palette, toast system (kinds, expiry, Reduce Motion persistence), modal stack with aria-hidden siblings, Home title row and read-status line placeholder.\n4. React root switches on `ui_variant`; legacy shell unchanged; existing feature views mount inside the new shell as-is where they already exist.\n5. Fixtures for boards R2Palette, R2Tenants, R2Dark; copy.ts for the shell.\n\n## Required acceptance\n\n- Invariants I8, I9, I10 with tests V2-T09, T10, T11 and native checks V2-N03, N04, N05.\n- Minimum window 1180×720; no horizontal scroll at 1180 wide at 200% zoom.\n- T09 native keyboard/focus/accessibility checks for every changed UI; the four accessibility additions in DESIGN-V2 §8 are in `native-checks.json` for C28.\n- Screenshot evidence set at 100% and 200% in both themes under `evidence/C28/screens/`.\n\n## Evidence and completion\n\nController runs, native record, screenshots, Codex review (D034: may complete at 8 with no blockers; raised to 9 before P09 review).\n\n## Safety and recovery\n\nFlag defaults to `legacy` in the production identity until C34; fixture identity may default to `v2`.\n# C29 — First-run wizard and add-tenant sheet\n\nPhase: P09. Status: planned. Required predecessor: C28.\n\n## Outcome\n\nA first-run user is taken from welcome to a verified tenant with credentials in the vault, selected products, optional starter packs and optional Academy account; an existing user adds a tenant through the same component in add mode. Realises D013.\n\n## Inputs and dependency gates\n\nC28; screens/wizard.md. Read the [common execution contract](../IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md),\n[review protocol](../review-protocol.md), and [test catalogue](../test-catalogue.md).\nRead the [UI v2 specification](../../architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md) and its\ncompanions; the frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is\nan immutable input. Freeze all source/shared dependency inputs.\n\n## Milestones\n\n1. Intents `verifyTenantSetup` (streaming `VerifyStep`, using existing reads per admitted product; unavailable products report \"not available\", never a result), `completeOnboarding`, `addTenant`; scan key required, management client and Gateway optional (D013, P17); secret entry only through the host secret sheet returning vault ids; v1 import offered as a secondary action on the tenant step.\n2. Wizard component with steps, validation (`aria-invalid`, `aria-describedby`, invalidation signature), rail context line, finite \"Open Prisma AIRS\", add mode (sheet 1160×780, 244px rail, Cancel semantics).\n3. Warnings from verify become Inbox items at completion (type defined here, rendered in C30).\n4. Fixtures for every R2On* board and R2AddTenant; copy.ts for the wizard including the welcome and trust text.\n\n## Required acceptance\n\n- `onboarding` transitions needed → inProgress → done; cancel in add mode writes nothing: the draft and its credentials are discarded (P27; stronger than the leftover credential the prototype assumed).\n- No intent persists, echoes or logs a secret: per P25 (accepted in C28) a secret enters once as `EnteredSecret` from the webview field and leaves it nowhere else; the host test on the mock runtime (`setup_draft_intents_cross_ipc_without_echoing_secrets_or_creating_tenants`) shows no receipt, snapshot or Keychain call carries it.\n- Unavailable products (AIS, AES) are not selectable and never verified; V2-T19 for the products step.\n- Live: verify against the designated read-only tenant (Vulture) under the owner scope, recorded as a redacted receipt; no writes.\n- T09 for every step; V2-N02.\n\n## Evidence and completion\n\nAs C28, plus the live verify receipt.\n\n## Safety and recovery\n\nStop on any unexpected tenant or authority state. Missing live access blocks the live row; it does not pass.\n# C30 — Inbox, reads, tenant switch guard, Home attention\n\nPhase: P09. Status: planned. Required predecessor: C29.\n\n## Outcome\n\nInbox items, reads and acknowledgments are core-owned per tenant; the single tenant-switch path refuses while a Harness decision is pending; Home shows attention and read status from the same scopes.\n\n## Inputs and dependency gates\n\nC29; screens/inbox-reads.md, screens/shell.md. Read the [common execution contract](../IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md),\n[review protocol](../review-protocol.md), and [test catalogue](../test-catalogue.md).\nRead the [UI v2 specification](../../architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md) and its\ncompanions; the frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is\nan immutable input. Freeze all source/shared dependency inputs.\n\n## Milestones\n\n1. Scopes `InboxItem`, `ReadStatus`; intents `readTenant`, `recheckProduct`, `acknowledgeItem`, `snoozeItem`, `unsnoozeItem`, `switchTenant{resolution?}` with `SwitchBlocked` refusal.\n2. Inbox screen (tabs, rows, detail pane, contextual action targets), Home attention list and read-status line, completion toasts derived from `ReadStatus` transitions, guard dialog rendered from the refusal.\n3. Snooze return times computed in core; one `snoozeLabel` shared by Home and Inbox.\n4. Fixtures for R2Inbox and the fresh-tenant state.\n\n## Required acceptance\n\n- Invariants I1, I2, I4, I11, I12 with V2-R01, R02, R04, R08, R09 and V2-T01, T02, T04, T12, T13; native V2-N01, N02.\n- Tenant-switch workload: new tenant's Home within 100 ms from cached scopes (registered in budgets.json).\n\n## Evidence and completion\n\nAs C28, plus the workload result.\n\n## Safety and recovery\n\nFixtures and mock runtime only; no live calls.\n# C31 — Reviews, Administration inventory, key rotation\n\nPhase: P09. Status: planned. Required predecessor: C30.\n\n## Outcome\n\nConfiguration reviews bind tenant, resource and typed name in the core; Administration renders from an inventory with per-tab capabilities; key rotation is a three-stage flow with one-time secret disclosure through the host.\n\n## Inputs and dependency gates\n\nC30; screens/reviews-administration.md. Read the [common execution contract](../IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md),\n[review protocol](../review-protocol.md), and [test catalogue](../test-catalogue.md).\nRead the [UI v2 specification](../../architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md) and its\ncompanions; the frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is\nan immutable input. Freeze all source/shared dependency inputs.\n\n## Milestones\n\n1. Scopes `Review`, `AdminInventory` (every tab mapped to an admitted `ManagementResource`/`GatewayRead`/C13 read and every action to an admitted `ChangeKind`+`ChangeAction`; AIS and AES unavailable with their gate), topic inventory with distinct detector/topic key types; intents `openReview`, `confirmReview{typed}`, `acknowledgeDeployment`; key rotation is the admitted sequence `ApiKeys·Version` → local acknowledgement → `ApiKeys·Delete` with readback; the issued secret uses the existing `RevealSecret`/`ForgetSecret` host path, is never persisted, and is dropped on every review exit including tenant switch and context retirement.\n2. Administration accordion and tables; review surface with diff, impact, typed name, applied panels; rotation panel states 1–4 (screens/reviews-administration.md); rotation reminder as a distinct Inbox item; two labelled timestamps (deployment acknowledged, old key removed) stored once; unknown outcomes shown as unconfirmed with reconciliation.\n3. Playground verdicts profile-aware with detector and topic results independent; applied topic examples classify under the topic.\n4. Fixtures for R2Admin and R2Review.\n\n## Required acceptance\n\n- Invariants I3, I6, I7 with V2-R03, R06, R07 and V2-T03, T06, T07, T08; V2-R10 (no mutation intent exists for an unavailable product) and V2-T19 (unavailable product renders no inventory and no action).\n- Known gaps 1–3 of DESIGN-V2 §10 closed with tests.\n- `AdminInventory` is generated from screens/administration-inventory.md and V2-T20 checks every (product, tab) disposition and action set (including Gateway keys: Rotate only, no staged rotation); V2-R11 pins the denied (kind, action) pairs including Gateway key Version; V2-T21 proves Red Team target names remain absent.\n- V2-R07 covers failed and unknown issuance and rejected and unknown deletion as named in screens/reviews-administration.md.\n- Live: one topic review apply and read-back against Redtail under the `airs-v2-c25-` prefix with cleanup, inside the owner scope. Key issuance and deletion are not run live in P09 (covered by C09 fixtures and C25 L-rows).\n\n## Evidence and completion\n\nAs C28, plus the live apply receipt and cleanup ledger.\n\n## Safety and recovery\n\nNo production destructive tests; stop on uncertain write outcome and record reconciliation.\n# C32 — Harness re-skin and lifecycle fixtures\n\nPhase: P09. Status: planned. Required predecessor: C31.\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe Harness renders in the new shell on the existing engine, sessions and decision model, with the three lifecycle fixtures as regression tests and contextual navigation for ended investigations.\n\n## Inputs and dependency gates\n\nC31; screens/harness.md. Read the [common execution contract](../IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md),\n[review protocol](../review-protocol.md), and [test catalogue](../test-catalogue.md).\nRead the [UI v2 specification](../../architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md) and its\ncompanions; the frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is\nan immutable input. Freeze all source/shared dependency inputs.\n\n## Milestones\n\n1. Harness screen in the layout rhythm: title row, conversation rail, transcript, composer, prerequisites checklist.\n2. Lifecycle fixtures blocks, mcp, keys in the contracts package with approve, decline, end and follow-up paths; all three are read-only tool calls (the mcp lifecycle reads `GatewayRead::McpServers`, P16; the keys lifecycle refuses to rotate and hands off, V2-T18). The existing C21 rule stands: the core decides from the tool's write flag whether the native confirmation sheet is required; no P09 fixture adds a write-capable call.\n3. `endConversation` seals the session and returns an archive id; transient hint for ended-conversation navigation; first send on a fresh tenant creates a user conversation.\n\n## Required acceptance\n\n- I1 pending-decision guard end to end (V2-N01), I12 (V2-T13); every lifecycle path tested; engine pin check unchanged.\n\n## Evidence and completion\n\nAs C28.\n\n## Safety and recovery\n\nFixture engine only; no live Harness runs (L16/L17 belong to C26).\n# C33 — API Client, Test Cases and the calls panel\n\nPhase: P09. Status: planned. Required predecessor: C32.\n\n## Outcome\n\nAPI Client and Test Cases render in the new shell with immutable response history, a live completion status, and the \"Show the calls\" panel reusing the response renderer.\n\n## Inputs and dependency gates\n\nC32; screens/api-client-test-cases.md. Read the [common execution contract](../IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md),\n[review protocol](../review-protocol.md), and [test catalogue](../test-catalogue.md).\nRead the [UI v2 specification](../../architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md) and its\ncompanions; the frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is\nan immutable input. Freeze all source/shared dependency inputs.\n\n## Milestones\n\n1. API Client re-skin; `role=\"status\"` completion region; history snapshots unchanged by later configuration (I5).\n2. Test Cases re-skin with pack-sourced cases from the wizard; Runtime-only \"Open in Playground\" hand-off and \"Inspect\" for every other product, which never dispatches a scan (V2-T15, P21).\n3. `show_calls` preference and side panel showing redacted request/response from diagnostics.\n4. Fixtures for R2Api and R2Cases.\n\n## Required acceptance\n\n- V2-R05, V2-T05, T14, T15, T16; known gap 5 closed; T09 for both screens; non-Runtime rows never dispatch a scan intent (mock runtime assertion).\n\n## Evidence and completion\n\nAs C28.\n\n## Safety and recovery\n\nFixtures only.\n# Prisma AIRS Desktop v2 implementation plan\n\nStatus: product interview decisions D001–D023 accepted; D024/D025 settle source\nterms and all four architecture candidates; D026 makes Codex the independent\nchunk and phase reviewer. G00/G01 passed; implementation proceeds from C01. A passing plan review is not a passing architecture,\nSDK, application, live-tenant, or package review.\n\n## Outcome and exclusions\n\nDeliver a fresh macOS Apple Silicon desktop application with React presentation\nin Tauri, a focused Rust application core, direct Rust SCM SDK integration, and\nthe native Rust Harness engine. Academy supplies shared presentation and remains\nthe authority for remote learning. Preserve agreed working v1 behavior, using\nv1 as requirements reference. Do not translate its GPUI implementation wholesale.\n\nNo desktop billing, media-generation backend, local MySQL/Redis server stack,\nNode/Bun backend runtime, TypeScript workers, speculative browser client, or\nin-app updater is included. Academy gamification remains inside Academy. Gateway\nusage/cost/budget/limits remain operational product functionality. Build-time\nJavaScript tooling and React WebView JavaScript are expected.\n\nSource destination: `ssh://git@git-ssh.cdot.io/cdot/prisma-airs-desktop-v2.git`.\nCheckout: `/Users/cdot/development/redtail/prisma-airs-desktop-v2`.\n\n## Architectural guiding principles\n\n1. Design deep modules: substantial behavior behind a small domain interface.\n   Apply the deletion test; do not wrap every SDK method in a pass-through module.\n2. The interface is the test surface. Exercise production transitions and\n   adapters; use independent wire/protocol expectations for external contracts.\n3. One adapter is a hypothetical seam; two real adapters justify a seam. Shared\n   Academy presentation has real web/desktop consumers. Do not build speculative\n   browser/backend/plugin architectures for this desktop delivery.\n4. Rust owns authority and locality for tenant/credential/workspace context,\n   request lifecycle, configuration review, protected storage, and approvals.\n   React owns presentation and editable input, not permission to execute.\n5. The SDK owns its declared transport/authentication contracts. The application\n   owns interactive identity, OS storage, context admission, and workflow policy.\n   Do not duplicate SDK retry/pagination/OAuth policy without a documented need.\n6. Unknown outcomes and partial/stale/denied/unsupported data remain distinct.\n   Never map an unknown verdict to allow or a cancelled write to successful rollback.\n7. Host credentials and capabilities are explicit. No ambient environment-file\n   discovery, inherited production fallback, generic renderer secret access,\n   unrestricted native plugin grants, or cross-origin credential forwarding.\n8. Shared appearance does not imply shared learner state. Tenant operations,\n   Academy identity/progression, Harness inference identity, and MCP grants stay\n   separately scoped. A tenant switch does not sign the learner out of Academy.\n9. Keep provenance and reproducibility local to dependency selection. Exact\n   versions, source hashes, build inputs, notices, and protocol pins are evidence;\n   a neighboring active worktree is not a release dependency.\n10. Measure native usability/performance and the actual installed package. A\n    successful browser render or mocked IPC assertion is insufficient evidence\n    for Tauri host behavior, VoiceOver, Keychain, sidecar isolation, or notarization.\n\nConcrete interfaces, crate decomposition, shared package extraction, and storage\nformats are outputs of G01. This plan defines behavior and testable work, not\nunreviewed Rust signatures or a predetermined hierarchy of tiny modules.\n\n## Ordered phases and chunks\n\nEvery Cxx has its own instruction file under [chunks](chunks/README.md). Complete\nchunks in numeric order. A dependency delay blocks its chunk; report it honestly\nand continue only research/preparation explicitly within that chunk. Do not\nsilently advance a later phase or replace a real dependency with a fake to pass.\nFor a prolonged upstream stall, report the exact dependency and offer an owner\nreorder/scope decision. Do not wait indefinitely or reorder silently; an approved\nchange updates predecessors, plan and review evidence before execution.\n\n| Phase | Chunks   | Result                                                           |\n|-------|----------|------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| P00   | G00, G01 | Confirmed plan; selected and reviewed architecture               |\n| P01   | C01–C03  | Shared desktop shell, native core, first complete Runtime scan   |\n| P02   | C04–C07  | Academy identity, learner presentation, assessment, offline work |\n| P03   | C08–C12  | Runtime/DLP administration, Sessions, reports, Library           |\n| P04   | C13–C15  | Existing Red Team/Model reads and complete API Client workflows  |\n| P05   | C16–C18  | Gateway workspace/configuration, reviewed changes, inference     |\n| P06   | C19–C22  | Native Harness, Rust sign-in, typed host tools, workspace MCP    |\n| P07   | C23–C24  | Reviewed imports, native quality, accessibility/privacy closure  |\n| P08   | C25–C26  | Controlled live qualification; signed installed DMG acceptance   |\n| P09   | C27–C44  | UI v2 \"Refined Native\": spec, shell, wizard, destinations (D058); re-cut from C35 as one screen per chunk ported from the prototype (D059) |\n\n### G00 — Plan confirmation\n\nFinish the decision ledger, baseline coverage, chunk instructions, review/test\nprotocols, dependency gates, and architecture handoff. Obtain an actual independent\nplan review meeting D019. Product decisions are accepted and the owner explicitly\nselected the architecture candidates and source terms in D024/D025. Continue the\nrequested design work; no further blanket scope question is needed. Architecture\nreview and implementation evidence remain distinct gates.\n\n### G01 — Architecture improvement workflow\n\nFollow [the handoff](architecture-handoff.md) and the requested\nimprove-codebase-architecture skill. Explore the named areas, show a temporary\nHTML report with before/after candidates, ask the owner to choose, and grill the\nselected design. Produce ADRs, interface/test ownership, dependency/import\ndecisions, and concrete chunk command specifications. Review the architecture\nat least 9/10 in every critical dimension and overall. Revise this plan if the\nselected design affects it, then re-review affected planning evidence.\n\nNo application scaffolding, shared-source refactoring, real-data migration,\nproduct endpoint calls, or packaging implementation begins before G01 passes.\n\n## Per-chunk execution contract\n\n1. Read AGENTS/CLAUDE, glossary, accepted ADRs, the chunk, predecessor receipts,\n   dependency manifest, test catalogue, and its canonical implementer prompt.\n2. Confirm a clean approved source snapshot and identify unrelated user work.\n   Resolve dependency availability/provenance and baseline check limitations.\n3. Implement only that chunk and approved supporting changes. A shared Academy,\n   SDK, or Harness change needs its own reviewed revision and regression evidence;\n   preserve active work and do not move another project's main branch casually.\n4. Run exact checks from the approved command manifest. Use deterministic local\n   fixtures and literal external contracts, then the appropriate native tests.\n   Never call hosted application endpoints by accident.\n5. Record commands, environments, inputs, results, failures, hashes, limitations,\n   and rollback rehearsal. Save raw sensitive evidence privately; commit redacted\n   summaries with references/hashes, not credentials or customer bodies.\n6. Freeze source and dependency inputs. Request actual independent Codex\n   review through [the independent prompt](prompts/review-chunk.md) (D026).\n7. If any critical dimension/overall score is below 9, required fixes remain,\n   source changed, or mandatory evidence is absent: remediate, rerun affected\n   checks, freeze a new snapshot, and request a new review of the same chunk.\n8. Complete only after the receipt and evidence validate against current inputs.\n   After a phase's last chunk, obtain the cumulative Codex phase review\n   ([prompt](prompts/review-phase.md)) before starting the next phase.\n   Make a focused commit; revalidate that its tree matches the reviewed tree.\n   Later edits invalidate affected receipts and trigger targeted regression\n   checks/re-review. Preserve failed attempts; never pressure a reviewer to pass.\n\n## Command contract to establish in C01\n\nThese commands are a required future interface, not tools that exist today:\n\n```text\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- check --chunk Cxx --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- test --chunk Cxx --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- native --chunk Cxx --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- review --chunk Cxx --reviewer codex --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- review --phase Pxx --reviewer codex --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- complete --chunk Cxx --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- package --kind preview --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- package --kind release-candidate --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\n```\n\nC01 creates the controller and a versioned manifest of exact commands, working\ndirectories, targets, features, fixtures, timeouts, and expected evidence. It\ncannot implement the later chunks itself. G01 specifies actual Rust/pnpm/Tauri\ncommands after choosing the workspace; a future engineer must not guess them or\nclaim these placeholder commands already ran. Document/test the controller's\nrejection of missing, stale, malformed, edited, or sub-threshold receipts.\n\n## Coverage and evidence\n\n- [Feature baseline](feature-baseline.md): existing working/preview/stub behavior.\n- [Parity matrix](parity-matrix.md): work ownership and release closure.\n- [Dependency gates](dependencies.md): accepted inputs and unresolved qualification.\n- [Test catalogue](test-catalogue.md): named behavioral/native/artifact test cases.\n- [Review protocol](review-protocol.md): scoring, receipt fields, invalidation.\n- [Release contract](release-contract.md): live scope, signing, package/install proof.\n- [Mandatory live checks](live-checks.md): fixed L-family/F-smoke requirements and\n  owner-approved per-workflow live scope; no access-driven silent reductions.\n- [Distribution gate](distribution.md): owner-selected source/binary terms,\n  Academy permission, framework disposition and exact shipped notices.\n- [Status](status.md): authoritative current state; planned is not implemented.\n\nG01 must convert each chunk's named tests into exact invocation commands and\nobservable assertions. Tests cannot simply repeat implementation decisions.\nFresh signed-artifact checks bind the final DMG hash and installed bytes; source\nor fixture checks do not substitute for them.\n\n## Expected sequencing dependencies\n\nThe scan proof can use accepted SDK Phase 3 after native macOS qualification.\nManagement/DLP uses accepted Phase 4 or a later explicitly reviewed compatible\npin. Existing Red Team/Model reads need verified Phase 5 capabilities; complete\nGateway needs Phase 6 capabilities. Harness/Academy transports are application\nwork, not delivered by the SCM SDK. Keep these upstream dependencies visible and\ndo not require unrelated SDK operations merely because they share a library.\n\nFirst-slice metrics establish named budgets before C04. Every UI chunk includes\nkeyboard/focus checks. Later introducing chunks register their numeric workload\nbudgets before implementation/acceptance measurement under T20 governance; budget\nchanges need recorded rationale and owner or independent reviewer acknowledgement.\nC24/C26 compare these pre-registered values, not newly fitted limits. C24 closes\nthe full native/VoiceOver/performance and cross-feature offline matrix.\nPreview packages may demonstrate accepted scope but must name missing features.\nOnly C26 can establish stable installed-package readiness.\n\n## Completion and delivery\n\nStable v2 requires every agreed working-v1 parity row closed, all chunk/phase\nreviews passing, designated live acceptance complete, no missing mandatory\nchecks, and C26's installed signed/notarized DMG evidence. V1 stays available;\nfresh credentials and reviewed imports remain explicit. Updates initially use\nmanual signed DMGs with rollback instructions.\n\nThe active implementation task may deliver reviewed Git commits to the exact\nowner-specified remote using normal pushes. Application release publication,\nhosting changes, and promotion over v1 must remain within the owner's explicit\nrelease instruction; preparing a signed package does not by itself publish it.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
