iew attempt-01: deferrals and a waived cleanup\n2344:## D056 — Academy live follow-ups move to 2.1.0; stable is 2.0.0\n2363:## D057 — C26 attempt 01: installed-acceptance defects and the Git rule\n2391:## D058 — UI v2 \"Refined Native\": frozen prototype, P09 extraction plan\n2451:## D059 — P09 re-cut: port the prototype, one gate per screen at 8\n2477:## Directions explicitly requested before round 1\n2490:## Interview exit and remaining evidence\n2502:## D060 — No import from the alpha; this desktop is v1\n{\n  \"request_id\": \"P09-attempt-01-1793649895\",\n  \"attempt_id\": \"attempt-01\",\n  \"subject\": \"P09\",\n  \"fingerprints\": {\n    \"source\": \"2ced3ba55ff87ea3652028dc3c25937375322eaafef4b6956e1e3133afeca265\",\n    \"dependencies\": \"b35a8d04c49e040dd8cc5b69a1825fbfaa21962b0fac55b64147e1206aed5628\",\n    \"build_flags\": \"166488b352224eb230ddfca178064d76f43deecbb6c73fb6d9359f56632e1a1f\",\n    \"evidence\": \"faa63b41870df92ead981cce70edf1b1a89973a1c5caaa7fe0b024e2bbde4377\"\n  },\n  \"scores\": {\n    \"architecture\": 9,\n    \"behavior\": 8,\n    \"authority_security\": 8,\n    \"validation\": 8,\n    \"overall\": 8\n  },\n  \"required_fixes\": [\n    \"R1 — API Client mutation reviews escape the integrated renderer-retirement boundary. apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/lib.rs:133 calls AuthorityHandle::retire_renderer on main-page reload, but crates/desktop-core/src/authority/change_domain.rs:909 retires only change-domain reviews and disclosures, leaving workbench.sending.review intact. Meanwhile authority/workbench_domain/send.rs:929 uses confirm without revocable ownership; NativeConfirmation::confirm supplies an independently live default lease (native_confirmation.rs:264). Consequently, an API Client Apply awaiting native confirmation can survive a renderer reload and, if accepted with unchanged context/files/credentials, pass check_review and dispatch the mutation. Context retirement or dismissReview removes the review but also leaves its queued/shown native sheet unowned. This defeats the lifecycle guarantee implemented for Administration and Harness. Acceptance: bind API Client review/confirmation presentation to revocable native ownership; retire it on renderer teardown, review dismissal/replacement, collection departure and context retirement; suppress queued stale sheets and reject late acceptance while preserving outcomes of requests already dispatched. Add production Host/IPC regressions covering both queued and shown confirmations, zero writes after retirement, and successful explicit fresh-page review.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"evidence_gaps\": [\n    \"E1 — The retained renderer_review_lifecycle tests cover change-domain confirmations and disclosures; the Harness regressions cover conversation retirement. Neither those tests nor the C41 native driver exercise an API Client mutation confirmation across main-page teardown. Passing these separate suites therefore does not establish the combined lifecycle property in R1. Retain a causal regression for that production path and its passing remediation evidence.\"\n  ],\n  \"optional_suggestions\": [],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Recomputed all four fingerprints. All 1,156 source and 15,928 evidence entries matched their frozen content, modes and symlink targets initially and at final recheck; source membership also matched.\",\n    \"Independently verified complete compiled-input membership and all 18,348 hashes, identical build/check before-and-after inventories, all 18 check-log hashes, predecessor-record bindings, the current executable and complete 1,621-entry bundle. Hash consistency does not authenticate execution or authorship.\",\n    \"All 20 mapped native drivers have their required passing targets bound to executable d8bf6a0f91507b6643a9888169873fe5c8bc1c96739bc2cd33b61aa3805ebcca. Superseded C24-N06 remains distinguishable from passing requirements. Inspected representative retained screenshots.\",\n    \"Independently ran 21 read