cation files were changed, endpoints called, real credentials accessed or OS permissions granted. C26/P08 controller and release gates remain separate. The read-only sandbox prevents writing the designated artifact; this returned JSON is the verdict.\"\n  ]\n}\ndocs/planning/reviews/C32/attempt-23/verdict-returned.json {\n  \"required_fixes\": [],\n  \"evidence_gaps\": [],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Verified all 8,242 scoped file hashes, complete compiled-input membership and 18,348 hashes, matching before/after inventories, build flags and all 18 check-log hashes. Hash consistency does not authenticate compiler execution or evidence authorship.\",\n    \"Verified the sealed source transition, current executable, complete bundle including executable modes and symlink targets, six frozen prototype files and bundled Harness engine pin. The reviewed G10 qualification uses aarch64-apple-darwin and test-fixtures; signed installed-release acceptance is separate.\",\n    \"The C32 fix carries admission-time revocable ownership through ConfirmHarness into confirm_scoped, revokes before dismissal and retains private settlement revalidation. Inspected both production-interface race regressions and native Cancel/Allow controls. Retained current logs report all eight Harness integration tests passing; I did not independently rerun Rust, renderer or GUI suites.\",\n    \"The original loopback old-red log records both intended stale-sheet assertion failures. The separate sandbox bind failures and initial green-build borrow-check failure remain distinguishable. No contemporaneous complete old-red worktree seal exists; that historical limitation does not establish an exact fully hashed old-red snapshot.\",\n    \"Verified bindings and required passing evidence across all 20 current native drivers. Read C32/C38 acceptance records, retained AX trees and representative captures covering project selection, approvals, switch guards, proposal review, ending, keyboard access, zoom and Reduce Motion. The superseded raw C24-N06 failure remains preserved.\",\n    \"Native evidence uses the real pinned engine with synthetic services, fixture folder selection and WKWebView captures. Native interactions, AppKit scheduling and spoken VoiceOver output were not independently exercised in this review.\",\n    \"Independently ran 21 read-only tests successfully: four Harness source-boundary tests, five C32 coverage-contract tests and twelve administration coverage tests. Current Gateway detail AX trees show successful scoped service/user-key details with Edit, Rotate, Remove and Close details; failed or loading panels cannot satisfy that evidence contract.\",\n    \"Verified C31 attempt-07's actual all-nine verdict, receipt, audit and preserved original scope. The shared-authority projection limits current differences to declared C32 Harness branches. The final C31 review cap was honored; no owner override activation or additional C31 review was inferred.\",\n    \"C30 remains owner-complete under its exact exception, with its independent 9/9/9/8/8 fail verdict and closed findings unchanged. G9, C29 live qualification and C30 timing remain historical. L19 retains three charged reads and zero remaining allowance; C26/P08 and release gates remain separate.\",\n    \"No application files were changed, endpoints called, real credentials accessed or OS permissions granted. The read-only sandbox prevents the designated artifact write; this returned JSON is the verdict.\"\n  ]\n}\ndocs/planning/reviews/C30/attempt-12/verdict-returned.json {\n  \"required_fixes\": [\n    \"R1 \\u2014 tools/native-acceptance/legacy_assertions.py:330 and tools/native-acceptance/acceptance_c37.py:366: the replacement for C30-N03 drops its mandatory capture matrix. docs/architecture/native-checks.json requires every hold-workflow step captured in light and dark at 100% and 200%; the current driver exercises holds once, then captures ordinary populated layouts separately. Current C36/C37