h those unperformed native assertions.\"\n  ],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Reproduced all four supplied fingerprints. All 5,108 scoped hashes matched initially and at final recheck. Independently checked membership and content of all 18,338 compiled-input entries, matching build/check seals, build flags and all 18 check-log hashes. These establish consistency, not compiler execution or evidence authorship.\",\n    \"Verified C29 attempt-10's receipt hash, request/verdict bindings, passing scores and unchanged scoped inventory. C28 and C27 receipt-to-verdict bindings also matched. No controller, phase or release completion is inferred.\",\n    \"The attempt-11 persistence-order finding is remediated: both switch paths save staged Data before destructive resolution and authority retirement. Inspected all four real-Harness save-failure regressions, original failing logs and current passing logs, including preservation, storage recovery, consumed-resolution refusal and Archive/Discard history outcomes. Those regressions were not independently rerun.\",\n    \"Independently executed the retained ui_v2_shell binary: 5/5 passed. In-memory execution of the production shell store passed captured-null retirement, late-delivery rejection, refusal replacement and tenant-toast retirement probes. The retained binary was not rebuilt or independently authenticated against compiler inputs. Broader results rely on retained logs, including 550 renderer tests, 17 Inbox tests and 22 Harness-tool tests.\",\n    \"Recomputed the complete 1,621-entry mode-aware fixture-bundle hash, executable hash and identifier. Its only executable files are the desktop application and pinned Rust Harness. Inspected 27 current C36/C37/C38 AX trees, ten historical C30 trees, observations and representative captures. Native interactions and spoken VoiceOver were not independently repeated.\",\n    \"Accept the documented method-02 presentation/guest rationale for this scoped performance gate. Verified all 12 raw switches, two fixed warmups, ten alternating measured samples, post-switch AX trees, current bindings and unchanged synthetic management-request count. Recomputed p95 is 23.69475 ms against 100 ms. No physical-host performance is established.\",\n    \"Verified historical L19 receipt and executable bindings. L19 remains historical production-adapter debug evidence, not live qualification of current bytes. Actual HTTP counts and private authorization were not independently observed.\",\n    \"No application files were changed, endpoints called, real credentials accessed or OS permissions granted. The read-only sandbox prevents the designated artifact write; this returned JSON is the verdict.\"\n  ]\n}\ndocs/planning/reviews/C41/attempt-09/verdict-returned.json {\n  \"required_fixes\": [\n    \"R1 \\u2014 apps/desktop/src/v2/workbench/api-client.tsx:178\\u2013188, especially the doc.id shortcut at line 186: returning to a request can remount an obsolete DocumentView. RequestEditor owns newer fields/revisions internally, while the parent retains its original document. Reproduced against the production component in memory: edit A's URL, receive successful protection, select B and lose its load observation, then select A. The URL reverted from /edited to /topics and A had only one openRequest call. Save can then remove the protected draft because those old fields equal the saved baseline (workbench_domain.rs:1828\\u20131839); Send can use the old request. Reload the authoritative document when returning after its editor unmounts, or retain an up-to-date document without reviving an obsolete snapshot. Acceptance: regression tests cover A edited/protected or saved, B's load pending/refused/undelivered, and return to A; latest fields and revision survive and explicit Save/Send receive them, with no automatic send.\",\n    \"R2 \\u2014 apps/desktop/src/v2/workbench/tools-sheet.tsx:242 and 251: schema-open replies unconditionally replace the editor even after a newer editor action. Reproduced against ToolsSheet in memory: hold openSchema(existing.json), create draft.json, type {\\\"newWork\\\":true}, then release the old result. The draft editor disappeared and was replaced by existing.json's text; the unsaved work was lost. Bind loads to the current editor generation and retire them on New, Close, or another selection. The environment loader at lines 94\\u2013102 has the same unguarded replacement pattern and needs equivalent protection. Acceptance: deferred opens superseded by a new schema, closing the editor, or a newer environment/schema selection cannot reopen or replace the current editor or its typing; add component regressions alongside the save-reply tests.\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_gaps\": [],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Full test suites and native UI were not rerun by this reviewer. Retained attempt-09 logs report 44 frontend files/645 tests passing, the full desktop-core fixture suite passing, and all three ui_v2_api tests passing. Two additional read-only, in-memory React/jsdom probes reproduced R1 and R2 using the current production components and scripted results; no application source or test files were changed.\",\n    \"Verified all 444 scoped file hashes and all 18,333 retained build/test input hashes against current bytes, the before/after inventory digests, every attempt-09 run-log hash, the evidence and build-flags digests, and the prepared fixture executable hash. These checks establish consistency of retained evidence, not independent proof of its execution or authorship; the supplied source aggregate is echoed.\",\n    \"Native assessment uses retained AX trees and fixture captures, including both parity composites and the 200% layout evidence. Product endpoints and credentials were not accessed. Native evidence is synthetic/loopback only, and spoken VoiceOver output was not recorded.\",\n    \"The predecessor is the supplied C40 pre-gate commit 73048f76 under the packet's recorded owner dependency amendment. This verdict does not establish integrated predecessor remediation, C26 completion, or cumulative P09 acceptance; unrelated owner work remains outside scope.\",\n    \"The review uses the packet's manual fresh-review transport; controller receipts and ledger completion are separate.\",\n    \"The atomic verdict-file write was denied by the read-only sandbox. This returned JSON is the verdict for controller persistence.\"\n  ]\n}\nC31 request keys ['c31_final_review_policy', 'request_id', 'attempt_id', 'subject', 'base_commit', 'transport', 'scope', 'predecessors', 'owner_decisions', 'fingerprints', 'fingerprint_notes', 'commands', 'native_acceptance', 'limitations', 'verdict_schema', 'verdict_path', 'review_instructions', 'source_transition']\nC31 live []\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
